// A module-level `comptime` constant, which is the shape that got past the rule once already.
// `_moduleConsts` folds the VALUE and records no type, and `exprClass` — the only classifier that reached
// a module static — filtered it through `isClass`, so a static of PRIMITIVE type answered "unknown". The
// rule is silent on an unknown source by design (it cannot tell a real negative from `constValue`'s int64
// reinterpretation of a magnitude above INT64_MAX), so this compiled and the C said 255.
//
// `moduleStaticCTypeRaw` is the unfiltered lookup, the same extraction `indexElemTypeRaw` is.
comptime int32 NEG = -1;
fn int32 main() {
    uint8 u = NEG;
    return cast<int32>(u);
}
